A||||11||Fiero_24||Car loses all power and backfires, Please help||||5||
Z||000000||Fiero_24||07-17-2001||11:04 AM||||I was on my way back from WI to IL, and my car just lost all power.  I pulled over and I heard a nice backfire.  Well I let it sit and I was back on the road.  Then it died again, and again, and finally I parked it and came back for it when it was cool.  I drove it for 30 minutes at 35mph, and then 10 minutes at 55mph, and it died again.  Last night I finally got it home as it died in my parking lot.  I had a new cat converter put on this morning since the old one rattles, but I drove it for 3 miles and now it will turn over but not start.  The car always had a slight hessitation during driving, like a misfire or something.  Has anyone had any problems like this?  I just replaced the wires, distributor cap and rotor, ignition coil, cat converter, spark plugs.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||5
Z||000001||Tom88gt||07-17-2001||11:10 AM||||What did the old cat look like?  Was it breaking up?  If so, your muffler may be plugged.||||reg||1
Z||000002||84Bill||07-17-2001||11:26 AM||||Ignition Module||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fiero_24||07-17-2001||11:59 AM||||The cat was all plugged, but looked solid inside.  I think I would at least get it to fire if there was something in the exhaust.  I cannot even get it to fire at all.  I am going to get an ignition module today.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||11
Z||000004||84Bill||07-17-2001||02:53 PM||||Ignition Modules are a bit on the pricey side so make sure your not getting spark before you get it. I should have asked this first before recomending.. But what year and engine type do you have?<P>2 thing to check for right off the bat are Fuel and Spark<P>take the top cover off and crank the engine a few times and smell for gas, look at the butterfly. If it's dry then you have no gas.<P>If you have fuel then check for spark. Pull a plug wire off and hold it about 1/8th inch from a bare metal spot on the engine and have someone crank the engine. you should see a nice little arc.<P>If not there could be a any number of things wrong but usually Ignition Modules are the culprit particularly if it was spitting and backfireing beforehand.||||reg||14
Z||000005||Fiero_24||07-17-2001||03:21 PM||||Well the car is in a parking lot and I need to try whatever it takes.  Ignition modules are $26 new at autozone, and I will have mine in a few hours.  I am going to try that, and then I guess I will call a tow truck.  I have an 87 GT 2.8 V6.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||9
Z||000006||84Bill||07-17-2001||03:30 PM||||Heh <BR>ok then it's a bit harder to tell if you getting fuel but if you crank it enough you will smell gas.<P>BTW<BR>Nice web page, I'll add a link to it from my site.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <A HREF="http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/fiero</A> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 07-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Fiero_24||07-17-2001||05:19 PM||||Thanks for the compliment and the link 84Bill.  My girlfriend just got home with the new Module.  I am going to go and put it on in an hour or so.  I am just praying that my next post will be to tell you that it runs again.  <P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||10
Z||000008||Tom88gt||07-17-2001||05:24 PM||||Could also be the coil.  BTW, Auto Zone sells rebuilt distributors that include a new ignition module for $99 with a 99 month warranty.  I don't know if the ignition module purchased alone has any warranty.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Fiero_24||07-17-2001||09:06 PM||||Well I got the new module and went back to try it.  I first tried it again without the new module, and nothing.  I then put the new module in and it fired up instantly.  I have yet to drive it home since traffic was so bad, but I drove it in the parking lot and it drove smooth.  The real test will be tonight to get it home.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||3
Z||000010||Fiero_24||07-18-2001||08:27 AM||||Bingo!!!!!!!  It was the module.  The car has so much more speed now, and no more hessitation.  I stomped on the gas and it took off like a rocket.  I did replace the coil, but the module went from all the heat coming from a bad cat converter.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||6
Z||000011||84Bill||07-18-2001||09:55 AM||||Yep the heat will kill a module. Glad you got it running again  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
